{"name":"Black River Falls","hex":"#343e54","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Black River Falls","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city, the county seat of Jackson County, Wisconsin, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Black_River_Falls"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black River Falls (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Black River Falls is the second album from Cathal Coughlan. It was released in October 2000 on Cooking Vinyl Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/40/Black_River_Falls_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_River_Falls_(album)","wikidata":"Q4921655"},{"title":"Black River Falls, Wisconsin","blocks":[{"text":"Black River Falls is a city in Jackson County, Wisconsin, United States, and its county seat. The population was 3,523 at the 2020 census. It is located along the Black River and home to the headquarters of the Ho-Chunk Nation of Wisconsin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Black_River_Falls_dam_and_hydro_plant.jpg/330px-Black_River_Falls_dam_and_hydro_plant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_River_Falls%2C_Wisconsin","wikidata":"Q267144"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River","wikidata":"Q4022"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/WS_7_I94_FHWA_1967_784.jpg/500px-WS_7_I94_FHWA_1967_784.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/WS_7_I94_FHWA_1967_784.jpg/1280px-WS_7_I94_FHWA_1967_784.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/WS_7_I94_FHWA_1967_784.jpg/500px-WS_7_I94_FHWA_1967_784.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Intersection of U.S. Route 12/Wisconsin State Route 54 in downtown Black River Falls, bridge crossing the Black River in background (1967)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi